
/*
	File: Distinguishing Languages
	_______________________________________________________________________________

	Only the comments matching the language should be highlighted as such.


	Topic: Highlight Using "Code"

		No language is specified so it uses the generic syntax highlighter.

		--- Code
		string language = "Unspecified";
		// C comment
		# Perl comment
		-- SQL comment
		---


	Topic: Highlight Using "C"

		--- C
		char* language = "C";
		// C comment
		# Perl comment
		-- SQL comment
		---


	Topic: Highlight Using "Perl"

		--- Perl
		my $language = "Perl";
		// C comment
		# Perl comment
		-- SQL comment
		---


	Topic: Highlight Using "SQL"

		--- SQL
		DECLARE @language AS VARCHAR(50) = "SQL";
		// C comment
		# Perl comment
		-- SQL comment
		---


	Topic: Highlight Using "Pascal"

		--- Pascal
		language: string := "Pascal";
		# Perl comment
		// Pascal comment 1
		(* Pascal comment 2 *)
		{ Pascal comment 3 }
		-- SQL comment
		---


	Topic: Highlight Using "Text"

		The "text" keyword will cause it to be treated as plain text with no highlighting.

		--- Text
		string language = "Text";
		# Perl comment
		// Pascal comment 1
		(* Pascal comment 2 *)
		{ Pascal comment 3 }
		-- SQL comment
		---

*/